      "index": "b7c8",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1152673282,
      "version": 118,
      "versionNonce": 303932802,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1782251350132,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So partitioning is\ndividing your\nDataFrame into chunks\ndistributed across\ndifferent nodes in your\ncluster. Each partition\ncan be processed in\nparallel, which speeds\nthings up. You can\npartition by a specific\ncolumn using\nrepartition or\npartitionBy—this is\nuseful for optimizing\njoins and aggregations\nbecause Spark can keep\nrelated data together\non the same node,\navoiding expensive\nshuffles across the\nnetwork",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": "klFbL-sRqWq6TVdO2UnZW",
      "originalText": "So partitioning is dividing your DataFrame into chunks distributed across different nodes in your cluster. Each partition can be processed in parallel, which speeds things up. You can partition by a specific column using repartition or partitionBy—this is useful for optimizing joins and aggregations because Spark can keep related data together on the same node, avoiding expensive shuffles across the network",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
